The U.S. state of [[Wisconsin]] first required its residents to register their [[motor vehicle]]s and display [[Vehicle registration plate|license plate]]s in 1905. Plates are currently issued by the [[Wisconsin Department of Transportation]] (WisDOT) through its Division of Motor Vehicles. Front and rear plates are required for most classes of vehicles, while only rear plates are required for motorcycles and trailers.

